        {
            "number": 2,
            "revision": "674248939ce87386c0546a86e4abf6c592e5d09d",
            "parents": [
                "bb15616a2d8dd9fc2d2e24fdbfa0d776010a3cf5"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/50/88050/2",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Rex Fu",
                "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                "username": "tifu_amdeng"
            },
            "createdOn": 1772708847,
            "author": {
                "name": "Rex Fu",
                "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                "username": "tifu_amdeng"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not interested in this change.\n\n1. For FRUs that have an EEPROM, the EEPROM is a more complete view of presence.  We do not also need the GPIO.\n\n2. For FRUs that do not have an EEPROM, but can be detected by a presence pin, please use entity-manager's support for GPIO-based presence detect."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "Got it.\nI will switch to entity-manager's GPIO-based presence detection."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-anacapa/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/presence-event-logger",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please don't make new custom log events.  Only use log-create."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-anacapa/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/presence-event-logger",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "With entity-manager's GPIO-based presence detection, presence changes are already reflected through the DevicePresence object lifecycle, and gpio-presence-sensor already emits journal messages for the add/remove transitions.\n\nIf a formal event log is still required in addition to that, my understanding is that it would need to be handled by a separate daemon service observing the presence state change. However, I do not see an existing log-create event that accurately matches presence insertion/removal.\n\nWould the existing journal log be sufficient for this case, or is there an existing log-create event that would be more appropriate?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-anacapa/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/presence-event-logger",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Or add code to the GPIO-presence detect to create the events you think are necessary..."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-anacapa/recipes-phosphor/gpio/phosphor-gpio-monitor/presence-event-logger",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "Implemented in the GPIO presence detect path.\n\nUploaded as three Gerrit changes:\n- 88279: Configuration: add LogPresenceChange to GPIODeviceDetect | https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/88279\n- 88280: State: add generic presence state events | https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/88280\n- 88281: gpio-presence: add configurable presence event logging | https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/88281\n\nThis emits DevicePresent on DevicePresence creation and DeviceAbsent\non removal, gated by LogPresenceChange."
                }
            ],
